window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["fastapi"]=[{"id":"fastapi-f0001","card":"q-fastapi-001-1-fastapi-overview-and-setup","sec":"fastapi-s002","q":"In what two ways is FastAPI \"fast\"?","a":"<p>It is fast to develop (little code to a working server) and fast at runtime (it serves many requests efficiently).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0002","card":"q-fastapi-001-1-fastapi-overview-and-setup","sec":"fastapi-s002","q":"Does FastAPI implement its own web server? What does it use?","a":"<p>No. FastAPI speaks <strong>ASGI</strong>, and <strong>Uvicorn</strong> serves HTTP.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0003","card":"q-fastapi-001-1-fastapi-overview-and-setup","sec":"fastapi-s002","q":"What do Pydantic and OpenAPI do in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Pydantic handles validation and serialization. OpenAPI docs are created automatically and shown at <code>/docs</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0004","card":"q-fastapi-001-1-fastapi-overview-and-setup","sec":"fastapi-s002","q":"What does a minimal FastAPI health-check server look like?","a":"<p>It creates <code>FastAPI()</code>, ties a function to <code>GET /health</code> and returns a dict, which is auto-converted to JSON.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from fastapi import FastAPI\napp = FastAPI()\n@app.get(&#x27;/health&#x27;)\ndef health():\n    return {&#x27;errors&#x27;: None}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0005","card":"q-fastapi-001-1-fastapi-overview-and-setup","sec":"fastapi-s002","q":"Which packages does the FastAPI course list in <code>requirements.txt</code>?","a":"<p><code>dynaconf</code>, <code>fastapi[standard]</code> and <code>pillow</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dynaconf ~= 3.2\nfastapi[standard] ~= 0.112.0\npillow ~= 10.4</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0006","card":"q-fastapi-002-2-rest-http-and-json-fundamentals","sec":"fastapi-s003","q":"What is REST?","a":"<p>Representational State Transfer, a form of RPC. The client sends a request and the server replies. It works on collections of things and supports CRUD over HTTP, with JSON as the encoding.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0007","card":"q-fastapi-002-2-rest-http-and-json-fundamentals","sec":"fastapi-s003","q":"How do the CRUD operations map to HTTP verbs?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>CRUD</th><th>HTTP verb</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Create</td><td><code>POST</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Retrieve</td><td><code>GET</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Update</td><td><code>PUT</code> / <code>PATCH</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Delete</td><td><code>DELETE</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0008","card":"q-fastapi-002-2-rest-http-and-json-fundamentals","sec":"fastapi-s003","q":"Why does a REST developer still need to know HTTP and JSON details?","a":"<p>Frameworks hide the HTTP and JSON layers most of the time, but the details leak through.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0009","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"What is HTTP at the wire level?","a":"<p>A textual protocol over sockets. You can send a raw request with Netcat, for example <code>nc httpbin.org 80</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0010","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"What are the parts of an HTTP request?","a":"<p>The request line (verb, path, version), headers, an empty line, and the body.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0011","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"What is the only required HTTP request header?","a":"<p><code>Host</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0012","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"What does <code>Connection: close</code> do in a request?","a":"<p>It closes the connection after the response.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0013","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"What does <code>Content-Length</code> count?","a":"<p>Body bytes only, not the headers. In the Netcat example it is 75.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0014","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"What are the parts of an HTTP response?","a":"<p>The status line (<code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK</code>), headers, an empty line, and the body.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0015","card":"q-fastapi-003-http-protocol","sec":"fastapi-s004","q":"Which two HTTP status codes does the course name as common?","a":"<p><code>200</code> OK and <code>404</code> Not Found.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0016","card":"q-fastapi-004-json","sec":"fastapi-s005","q":"How do JSON types map to Python types?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>JSON</th><th>Python</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>object</td><td><code>dict</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>array</td><td><code>list</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>string</td><td><code>str</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>number</td><td><code>int</code> / <code>float</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>true/false</td><td><code>bool</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>null</td><td><code>None</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0017","card":"q-fastapi-004-json","sec":"fastapi-s005","q":"Which Python types have no JSON equivalent?","a":"<p><code>set</code> and <code>tuple</code>. JSON also has only one number type, while Python has <code>int</code>, <code>float</code>, <code>Decimal</code> and <code>Fraction</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0018","card":"q-fastapi-004-json","sec":"fastapi-s005","q":"What does JSON lack, and how are those values sent?","a":"<p>JSON has no <strong>datetime</strong> type, so it is sent as a string and the receiver must convert it. JSON has no <strong>binary</strong> type, so binary data is usually Base64.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0019","card":"q-fastapi-004-json","sec":"fastapi-s005","q":"Who does JSON encoding and decoding in a FastAPI server?","a":"<p>FastAPI does it for you.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0020","card":"q-fastapi-004-json","sec":"fastapi-s005","q":"How does a car record look as a JSON document in a FastAPI server (with a <code>null</code> and a list)?","a":"<p>It is a JSON object. <code>airport</code> is <code>null</code>, <code>tags</code> is an array and <code>shared</code> is a boolean.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n  &quot;car_id&quot;: &quot;CAR3&quot;,\n  &quot;lat&quot;: 0.7579787,\n  &quot;lng&quot;: -73.9881175,\n  &quot;passenger_count&quot;: 3,\n  &quot;shared&quot;: true,\n  &quot;tags&quot;: [&quot;shared&quot;, &quot;nyc&quot;],\n  &quot;airport&quot;: null,\n  &quot;timestamp&quot;: &quot;2024-01-02T13:42:09Z&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0021","card":"q-fastapi-005-3-handlers-running-the-server-sync-vs-as","sec":"fastapi-s006","q":"What is a handler in FastAPI?","a":"<p>A function that takes a request and returns a response. A decorator such as <code>@app.get('/path')</code> ties it to an HTTP verb and path. Returned dicts become JSON.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0022","card":"q-fastapi-006-running","sec":"fastapi-s007","q":"What are the two <code>fastapi</code> commands to run a server, and how do they differ?","a":"<p><code>fastapi run</code> is for production and has no auto-reload. <code>fastapi dev</code> is for development and reloads on file change.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>fastapi run Ch02/02_02/server.py    # production: no auto-reload\nfastapi dev Ch02/02_02/server.py    # development: reloads on file change</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0023","card":"q-fastapi-006-running","sec":"fastapi-s007","q":"How do you run a FastAPI app from code with <code>python server.py</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>uvicorn.run(app)</code> under the <code>__main__</code> guard. Uvicorn also takes a port, host and more.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if __name__ == &#x27;__main__&#x27;:\n    import uvicorn\n    uvicorn.run(app)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0024","card":"q-fastapi-006-running","sec":"fastapi-s007","q":"How do you test the <code>/health</code> endpoint from the command line?","a":"<p>Use <code>curl</code>, which returns <code>{\"errors\": null}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>curl http://localhost:8000/health</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0025","card":"q-fastapi-007-sync-vs-async-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s008","q":"What does FastAPI use for I/O-bound concurrency, and what is the risk?","a":"<p>It uses <strong>asyncio</strong>, which runs on a single thread. A blocking call inside an <code>async</code> handler blocks every request.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0026","card":"q-fastapi-007-sync-vs-async-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s008","q":"What happens with a sync handler that calls blocking <code>sleep(1)</code>?","a":"<p>It is fine. FastAPI runs sync handlers in a thread pool.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0027","card":"q-fastapi-007-sync-vs-async-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s008","q":"What happens with an <code>async</code> handler that calls blocking <code>sleep(1)</code>?","a":"<p>Never do this. It blocks the event loop and requests queue up.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0028","card":"q-fastapi-007-sync-vs-async-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s008","q":"What is the correct way to sleep in an <code>async</code> handler?","a":"<p>Use <code>await asyncio.sleep(1)</code>, which is non-blocking and concurrent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.get(&#x27;/sleep/async-aio&#x27;)\nasync def aio_sleep():\n    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n    return {&#x27;error&#x27;: None}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0029","card":"q-fastapi-007-sync-vs-async-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s008","q":"How long do 10 concurrent requests take for sync + <code>sleep</code>, async + <code>sleep</code> and async + <code>asyncio.sleep</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Handler</th><th>Total time</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>sync + <code>sleep</code></td><td>~1 s</td><td>thread pool</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>async + <code>sleep</code> (bad)</td><td>~10 s</td><td>event loop blocked, serialized</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>async + <code>asyncio.sleep</code></td><td>~1 s</td><td>non-blocking</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0030","card":"q-fastapi-007-sync-vs-async-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s008","q":"Should you start with sync or async handlers in FastAPI, and why?","a":"<p>Start with sync handlers and move to async only for performance reasons. A third-party library deep in the call chain may block without you knowing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0031","card":"q-fastapi-008-example-info-handler","sec":"fastapi-s009","q":"What does the FastAPI <code>/info</code> handler return?","a":"<p>The version, the current time and the running user. The <code>datetime</code> is auto-serialized to an ISO string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.get(&#x27;/info&#x27;)\ndef info():\n    return {\n        &#x27;version&#x27;: &#x27;0.1.0&#x27;,\n        &#x27;time&#x27;: datetime.now(tz=UTC),\n        &#x27;user&#x27;: environ[&#x27;USER&#x27;],\n    }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0032","card":"q-fastapi-008-example-info-handler","sec":"fastapi-s009","q":"What does <code>curl http://localhost:8000/info</code> return?","a":"<p>JSON such as <code>{\"version\":\"0.1.0\",\"time\":\"2024-01-02T13:42:09Z\",\"user\":\"vscode\"}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0033","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"How are query parameters written in a URL?","a":"<p>After <code>?</code>, separated by <code>&amp;</code>, for example <code>GET /logs?start=2024-01-01T00:00:00&amp;end=2024-01-02T00:00:00&amp;level=ERROR</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0034","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"How do FastAPI function parameters map to query parameters?","a":"<p>Function parameters become query parameters, and <strong>type hints</strong> drive conversion. A <code>datetime</code> is parsed from ISO.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0035","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"How do you make a query parameter optional in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Give it a default, such as <code>level: str = None</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0036","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"What happens when a query parameter fails type conversion?","a":"<p>FastAPI automatically returns <code>422 Unprocessable Entity</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0037","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"How do you report your own validation errors in a FastAPI handler?","a":"<p>Raise <code>HTTPException</code> with the right status.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raise HTTPException(\n    status_code=HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST, detail=&#x27;invalid log level&#x27;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0038","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"What checks does the <code>/logs</code> handler make on its parameters?","a":"<p>It checks that <code>start</code> is before <code>end</code> (400), that <code>level</code> is valid (400), and that records were found (404).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if start &gt;= end:\n    raise HTTPException(\n        status_code=HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST, detail=&#x27;start must be before end&#x27;\n    )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0039","card":"q-fastapi-009-query-parameters","sec":"fastapi-s010","q":"Where does FastAPI show its automatic OpenAPI documentation?","a":"<p>At <code>/docs</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0040","card":"q-fastapi-010-request-body-pydantic-models","sec":"fastapi-s011","q":"How do you validate a JSON request body in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Use a <strong>Pydantic</strong> model as the handler parameter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.post(&#x27;/sales/&#x27;)\ndef new_sale(sale: Sale):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0041","card":"q-fastapi-010-request-body-pydantic-models","sec":"fastapi-s011","q":"How do you add validation rules such as minimum length or greater-than to a Pydantic field?","a":"<p>Use <code>Field</code>. FastAPI validates it automatically, and failures give <code>422</code> with detailed messages.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>customer_id: str = Field(min_length=2)\namount: int = Field(gt=0)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0042","card":"q-fastapi-010-request-body-pydantic-models","sec":"fastapi-s011","q":"Why keep API models separate from DB models?","a":"<p>The layers may store data differently. In the sales example, the API uses dollars and the DB stores cents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>price=int(sale.price * 100),  # Convert dollars to cents for DB</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0043","card":"q-fastapi-010-request-body-pydantic-models","sec":"fastapi-s011","q":"What does a return annotation like <code>-&gt; Sale</code> add?","a":"<p>The response schema in <code>/docs</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0044","card":"q-fastapi-010-request-body-pydantic-models","sec":"fastapi-s011","q":"What is a path parameter in FastAPI?","a":"<p>A <code>{key}</code> in the route, bound to the <code>key</code> argument of the handler.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.get(&#x27;/sales/{key}&#x27;)\ndef get_sale(key: str) -&gt; Sale:</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0045","card":"q-fastapi-010-request-body-pydantic-models","sec":"fastapi-s011","q":"Which Pydantic type is mentioned for datetimes that must be in the past?","a":"<p><code>PastDatetime</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0046","card":"q-fastapi-011-html-forms","sec":"fastapi-s012","q":"How do browsers submit HTML forms, and how do you read the fields in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Browsers submit forms as <code>POST</code>. Use <code>Annotated[..., Form()]</code> for each field.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Annotated[str, Form()],</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0047","card":"q-fastapi-011-html-forms","sec":"fastapi-s012","q":"How does FastAPI serve static HTML files?","a":"<p>Mount <code>StaticFiles</code> on a path.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app.mount(&#x27;/static&#x27;, StaticFiles(directory=&#x27;static&#x27;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0048","card":"q-fastapi-011-html-forms","sec":"fastapi-s012","q":"How do you send the user to another page after a form submit?","a":"<p>Return a <code>RedirectResponse</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return RedirectResponse(\n    url=&#x27;/static/thanks.html&#x27;,\n    status_code=HTTPStatus.FOUND,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0049","card":"q-fastapi-011-html-forms","sec":"fastapi-s012","q":"What must the HTML side of a form match so FastAPI can read it?","a":"<p>The field names. The form uses <code>method=\"POST\"</code> and an <code>action</code> path, and each input's <code>name</code> matches a handler parameter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;/survey&quot;&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0050","card":"q-fastapi-012-raw-request-data","sec":"fastapi-s013","q":"How do you read the raw request body in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Add a <code>Request</code> parameter and call <code>await request.body()</code>. Reading the body needs <code>await</code>, so the handler must be <code>async</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>data = await request.body()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0051","card":"q-fastapi-012-raw-request-data","sec":"fastapi-s013","q":"Why check the size of a raw upload?","a":"<p>Never accept unbounded input from the internet. Read <code>Content-Length</code> and reject missing or oversized bodies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>size = int(request.headers.get(&#x27;Content-Length&#x27;, 0))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0052","card":"q-fastapi-012-raw-request-data","sec":"fastapi-s013","q":"How do you read a header from a FastAPI request?","a":"<p><code>request.headers.get('Header-Name')</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0053","card":"q-fastapi-012-raw-request-data","sec":"fastapi-s013","q":"What is <code>BytesIO</code> used for when handling raw bytes?","a":"<p>It turns raw bytes into a file-like object for libraries such as PIL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>io = BytesIO(data)\nimg = Image.open(io)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0054","card":"q-fastapi-012-raw-request-data","sec":"fastapi-s013","q":"In the FastAPI raw-request example, what does the <code>/size</code> endpoint return?","a":"<p>It reads the request body, opens it as an image with <code>Image.open</code>, and returns the image <code>width</code> and <code>height</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>data = await request.body()\nio = BytesIO(data)\nimg = Image.open(io)\nreturn {&#x27;width&#x27;: img.width, &#x27;height&#x27;: img.height}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0055","card":"q-fastapi-013-example-start-stop-a-vm-enum-lock-path-p","sec":"fastapi-s014","q":"What endpoints does the VM example define?","a":"<p><code>POST /vm/start</code> takes <code>cpu_count</code> (1-64), <code>mem_size_gb</code> (8-1024) and <code>image</code> (one of three), and returns an id. <code>POST /vm/{id}/stop</code> returns the id and spec, or 404.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0056","card":"q-fastapi-013-example-start-stop-a-vm-enum-lock-path-p","sec":"fastapi-s014","q":"How does Pydantic restrict a field to a fixed set of values?","a":"<p>Use an <strong>Enum</strong> field. Pydantic rejects values outside the allowed set.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Image(Enum):\n    ubuntu = &#x27;ubuntu:24.04&#x27;\n    debian = &#x27;debian:bookworm&#x27;\n    alpine = &#x27;alpine:3.20&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0057","card":"q-fastapi-013-example-start-stop-a-vm-enum-lock-path-p","sec":"fastapi-s014","q":"How are the VM <code>cpu_count</code> and <code>mem_size_gb</code> limits expressed?","a":"<p>With <code>Field</code> bounds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>cpu_count: int = Field(gt=0, lt=65)\nmem_size_gb: int = Field(ge=8, lt=1025)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0058","card":"q-fastapi-013-example-start-stop-a-vm-enum-lock-path-p","sec":"fastapi-s014","q":"Why does the VM example use a <code>Lock</code>?","a":"<p>It protects shared state, because sync handlers run in multiple threads.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with lock:\n    vms[id] = vm</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0059","card":"q-fastapi-013-example-start-stop-a-vm-enum-lock-path-p","sec":"fastapi-s014","q":"What does <code>vms.pop(id, None)</code> do?","a":"<p>It removes and returns the VM, or returns <code>None</code> if it is not there.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0060","card":"q-fastapi-013-example-start-stop-a-vm-enum-lock-path-p","sec":"fastapi-s014","q":"How does the VM example generate an id?","a":"<p><code>uuid4().hex</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>id = uuid4().hex</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0061","card":"q-fastapi-014-json-responses-with-pydantic","sec":"fastapi-s015","q":"What does returning a Pydantic model add compared to returning a dict?","a":"<p>Both give JSON. A Pydantic return type also adds the response schema to <code>/docs</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0062","card":"q-fastapi-014-json-responses-with-pydantic","sec":"fastapi-s015","q":"How does a <code>timedelta</code> serialize by default in a FastAPI response?","a":"<p>As an ISO 8601 duration, for example <code>\"PT1M27S\"</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0063","card":"q-fastapi-014-json-responses-with-pydantic","sec":"fastapi-s015","q":"How do you return a <code>timedelta</code> as seconds, such as <code>{\"delta\": 87}</code>?","a":"<p>Use a <strong>field serializer</strong> on the Pydantic model. Make its return type match what clients expect.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@field_serializer(&#x27;delta&#x27;)\ndef serialize_delta(self, v: timedelta) -&gt; int:\n    return int(v.total_seconds())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0064","card":"q-fastapi-015-streaming-responses","sec":"fastapi-s016","q":"When do you use <code>StreamingResponse</code> in FastAPI?","a":"<p>For large or incremental data. The handler passes a generator, and items are sent as they are produced without buffering everything.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return StreamingResponse(events)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0065","card":"q-fastapi-015-streaming-responses","sec":"fastapi-s016","q":"Can JSON be streamed?","a":"<p>JSON itself does not stream, but <strong>JSON Lines (NDJSON)</strong>, one JSON object per line, does.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0066","card":"q-fastapi-015-streaming-responses","sec":"fastapi-s016","q":"How does each item get written in the streaming events example?","a":"<p>The generator yields each event as a JSON line.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>yield event.model_dump_json() + &#x27;\\n&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0067","card":"q-fastapi-015-streaming-responses","sec":"fastapi-s016","q":"Which HTTP mechanism sits under streaming responses?","a":"<p><strong>Chunked transfer encoding</strong>: the chunk size in hex, then the data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0068","card":"q-fastapi-015-streaming-responses","sec":"fastapi-s016","q":"How do you inspect the raw chunked stream with curl?","a":"<p>Use <code>--raw</code> to keep the chunk framing and <code>-i</code> to show headers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>curl -i --raw http://localhost:8000/events?start=2024-08-06T14:18:30</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0069","card":"q-fastapi-016-raw-non-json-responses","sec":"fastapi-s017","q":"How do you return a non-JSON response such as an image in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Return a <code>Response</code> with <code>bytes</code> content and a <code>media_type</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return Response(\n    content=out.getvalue(),\n    status_code=HTTPStatus.OK,\n    media_type=&#x27;image/png&#x27;,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0070","card":"q-fastapi-016-raw-non-json-responses","sec":"fastapi-s017","q":"How are inputs passed to the <code>/resize</code> endpoint?","a":"<p><code>width</code> and <code>height</code> are query parameters, and the image is the request body. Validate both the size and the parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>async def resize(width: int, height: int, request: Request):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0071","card":"q-fastapi-016-raw-non-json-responses","sec":"fastapi-s017","q":"What does <code>/resize</code> check about width and height?","a":"<p>Both must be positive, otherwise it raises 400.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if width &lt;= 0 or height &lt;= 0:</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0072","card":"q-fastapi-016-raw-non-json-responses","sec":"fastapi-s017","q":"How does the <code>/resize</code> handler write the resized image to PNG bytes?","a":"<p>It saves to a <code>BytesIO</code> with <code>format='PNG'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>img = img.resize((width, height))\nout = BytesIO()\nimg.save(out, format=&#x27;PNG&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0073","card":"q-fastapi-017-custom-error-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s018","q":"What does FastAPI return for an exception type it does not know?","a":"<p><code>500 Internal Server Error</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0074","card":"q-fastapi-017-custom-error-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s018","q":"How do you register a custom error handler in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Use <code>@app.exception_handler(ExcType)</code> on an <code>async def (request, exc)</code> that returns a <code>JSONResponse</code> with custom status, content and headers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.exception_handler(FreqError)\nasync def freq_error_handler(request: Request, exc: FreqError):\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST,\n        content={&#x27;error&#x27;: str(exc)},\n        headers={&#x27;X-Frequency-Text&#x27;: request.query_params.get(&#x27;text&#x27;, &#x27;&#x27;)},\n    )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0075","card":"q-fastapi-017-custom-error-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s018","q":"What naming convention do custom HTTP headers follow, and are names case-sensitive?","a":"<p>Custom headers conventionally start with <code>X-</code>. Header names are case-insensitive.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0076","card":"q-fastapi-017-custom-error-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s018","q":"Why should you not put raw exception text in an error response?","a":"<p>It can leak tokens, addresses or other sensitive data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0077","card":"q-fastapi-017-custom-error-handlers","sec":"fastapi-s018","q":"In FastAPI, when does the <code>/freq</code> endpoint raise <code>FreqError</code>, and how does the registered handler turn it into a 400 response?","a":"<p><code>char_freq</code> raises <code>FreqError('empty text')</code> when the text is empty. The handler registered with <code>@app.exception_handler(FreqError)</code> returns a <code>JSONResponse</code> with status 400 and the error text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def char_freq(text: str):\n    if not text:\n        raise FreqError(&#x27;empty text&#x27;)</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.exception_handler(FreqError)\nasync def freq_error_handler(request: Request, exc: FreqError):\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST,\n        content={&#x27;error&#x27;: str(exc)},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0078","card":"q-fastapi-018-example-query-logs-with-content-negotiat","sec":"fastapi-s019","q":"What does the logs-query example return?","a":"<p>JSON by default, CSV if the request has <code>Accept: text/csv</code>, 404 if nothing matches, and 400 on bad input.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0079","card":"q-fastapi-018-example-query-logs-with-content-negotiat","sec":"fastapi-s019","q":"What is content negotiation?","a":"<p>The <code>Accept</code> header picks the response format. <code>*/*</code> means \"anything\", so default to JSON, and reject unsupported types with 400.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mime_type = req.headers.get(&#x27;Accept&#x27;, &#x27;application/json&#x27;)\nif mime_type == &#x27;*/*&#x27;:  # Client didn&#x27;t specify, default to JSON\n    mime_type = &#x27;application/json&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0080","card":"q-fastapi-018-example-query-logs-with-content-negotiat","sec":"fastapi-s019","q":"How do you build a CSV response in FastAPI?","a":"<p>Write with <code>csv.DictWriter</code> into a <code>StringIO</code>, use <code>datetime.isoformat()</code> for times, and return a <code>Response</code> with <code>media_type='text/csv'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>io = StringIO()\nwriter = csv.DictWriter(io, fieldnames=[&#x27;time&#x27;, &#x27;level&#x27;, &#x27;message&#x27;])\nwriter.writeheader()\nreturn Response(content=io.getvalue(), media_type=&#x27;text/csv&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0081","card":"q-fastapi-018-example-query-logs-with-content-negotiat","sec":"fastapi-s019","q":"How does the logs example validate <code>count</code> and <code>offset</code>?","a":"<p>It returns 400 when <code>count</code> is below 1 or <code>offset</code> is negative.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if count &lt; 1 or offset &lt; 0:\n    return Response(status_code=HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST, content=&#x27;bad count or offset&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0082","card":"q-fastapi-018-example-query-logs-with-content-negotiat","sec":"fastapi-s019","q":"How does the logs example pick between the JSON and CSV builders?","a":"<p>It selects a function by MIME type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>fn = json_response if mime_type == &#x27;application/json&#x27; else csv_response</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0083","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"What is the order of configuration layers in a FastAPI server?","a":"<p>Defaults in code, then a config file, then environment variables, then command-line arguments. Each layer overrides the previous one.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0084","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"Why use configuration?","a":"<p>The code stays the same while configuration changes behavior, such as the port, log level or auth server.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0085","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"How is Dynaconf set up?","a":"<p>In <code>config.py</code>, create <code>Dynaconf</code> with an env var prefix and settings files.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>settings = Dynaconf(\n    envvar_prefix=&#x27;SERVER&#x27;,\n    settings_files=[&#x27;settings.yaml&#x27;, &#x27;.secrets.yaml&#x27;],\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0086","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"What does <code>envvar_prefix='SERVER'</code> do?","a":"<p>Environment variables such as <code>SERVER_PORT=9999</code> are picked up.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0087","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"What goes in <code>.secrets.yaml</code>?","a":"<p>Secrets such as auth tokens. Keep it out of Git.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0088","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"How do you add a <code>--port</code> command-line argument with a config default?","a":"<p>Use <code>ArgumentParser</code> and default to <code>settings.port</code>, then update the settings.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>parser.add_argument(&#x27;--port&#x27;, type=int, default=settings.port)\nargs = parser.parse_args()\nsettings.update(vars(args))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0089","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"How do you override the port by CLI and by environment variable?","a":"<p>Pass <code>--port</code>, or set <code>SERVER_PORT</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python server.py --port 9999           # CLI overrides\nSERVER_PORT=9999 python server.py      # env var overrides</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0090","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"Why validate configuration, and how does the config server do it?","a":"<p>Bad config causes many production outages. The server exits if the port is outside the valid range.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if settings.port &lt; 0 or settings.port &gt; 65_535:\n    raise SystemExit(f&#x27;error: invalid port - {settings.port}&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0091","card":"q-fastapi-019-configuration","sec":"fastapi-s020","q":"In a FastAPI server using Dynaconf, what does <code>settings.yaml</code> hold and how does <code>python server.py</code> use it?","a":"<p>It holds the default <code>port</code>, and <code>python server.py</code> starts on port 8080 from it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>---\nport: 8080</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python server.py                       # settings.yaml (port 8080)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0092","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"Metrics vs logging: what question does each answer?","a":"<p>Metrics answer \"what is happening now?\" (request count, error rate, query latency). Logging answers \"how did we get here?\" (incidents, debugging).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0093","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"Which tools does the course name for metrics?","a":"<p>Prometheus, OpenTelemetry and Datadog.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0094","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"Which module does FastAPI code use for logging?","a":"<p>Python's built-in <code>logging</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0095","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"What should you ask about logging in a code review?","a":"<p>Should we log here, at what level, and with what info? Log enough to reproduce the problem, such as query parameters. Configure logging as early as possible, ideally from config.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0096","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"Why test your logs in development?","a":"<p>If logs don't help in development, they won't help during a 4 a.m. incident.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0097","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"How do you configure logging with level, format and date format?","a":"<p>Call <code>logging.basicConfig</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>logging.basicConfig(\n    level=logging.INFO,\n    format=&#x27;%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s&#x27;,\n    datefmt=&#x27;%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S&#x27;,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0098","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"What is middleware in FastAPI, and what does <code>call_next</code> do?","a":"<p>Middleware runs around every HTTP request. <code>call_next</code> invokes the next middleware or the handler.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.middleware(&#x27;http&#x27;)\nasync def timing(request: Request, call_next):\n    start = perf_counter()\n    response = await call_next(request)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0099","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"Why prefix metric log lines with something like <code>[metric:call.duration]</code>?","a":"<p>So a collector can parse and forward them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;[metric:call.duration] %s %s %d - %.2fs&#x27;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0100","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"How do you use Uvicorn's logger instead of the root logger?","a":"<p>Get the logger named <code>uvicorn</code>. This helps separate server logs from app logs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>log = logging.getLogger(&#x27;uvicorn&#x27;)\nlog.info(&#x27;message&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0101","card":"q-fastapi-020-logging-and-metrics","sec":"fastapi-s021","q":"In a FastAPI logging example, how does the <code>/posts/{login}</code> handler treat the <code>since</code> parameter?","a":"<p>If <code>since</code> is given, it is parsed with the format <code>'%Y%m%d'</code>. If not, it defaults to 7 days back. The handler then logs the request with <code>logging.info</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.get(&#x27;/posts/{login}&#x27;)\ndef get_posts(login: str, since: str = None):\n    if since:\n        since = datetime.strptime(since, &#x27;%Y%m%d&#x27;)\n    else:\n        since = datetime.now() - timedelta(days=7)\n        since = datetime(since.year, since.month, since.day)\n    logging.info(&#x27;get posts for %s since %s&#x27;, login, since)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0102","card":"q-fastapi-021-security","sec":"fastapi-s022","q":"Where should you start with application security?","a":"<p>The OWASP Top 10, which includes broken access control, cryptographic failures and injection.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0103","card":"q-fastapi-021-security","sec":"fastapi-s022","q":"What is the \"security hat\" mindset?","a":"<p>Developers think about how things should work. With the security hat on, ask how a malicious actor would abuse the code. In reviews ask what you should validate and what you are not checking.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0104","card":"q-fastapi-021-security","sec":"fastapi-s022","q":"What security problems does the insecure users server have?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Problem</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Broken access control</td><td>anyone can read user details or create users; no authn/authz</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>No input validation</td><td><code>login</code> not checked for malicious characters</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>No body size limit</td><td><code>set_icon</code> reads the whole body; attacker can send gigabytes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Can overwrite users</td><td><code>set_user</code> doesn't check existence</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>No admin check</td><td>creating users should require admin</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0105","card":"q-fastapi-021-security","sec":"fastapi-s022","q":"Which line in <code>set_icon</code> is the unbounded-input problem?","a":"<p>It reads the whole body with no size limit.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>data = await request.body()  # No size limit!</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0106","card":"q-fastapi-022-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"What two problems come up when using a database with the <code>fastapi</code> CLI?","a":"<p>There is no main function to connect to the DB, and each request needs its own cursor.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0107","card":"q-fastapi-022-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"What are FastAPI's answers to those two problems?","a":"<p><strong>Lifespan events</strong> (startup and shutdown) and <strong>dependency injection</strong> with <code>Depends</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0108","card":"q-fastapi-022-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"How do you create the <code>trades</code> SQLite database from <code>schema.sql</code>?","a":"<p>Remove the old file and load the schema with <code>sqlite3</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>rm -f trades.db\nsqlite3 trades.db &lt; schema.sql</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0109","card":"q-fastapi-022-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"What does the <code>trades</code> table look like?","a":"<p>It has time, user, symbol, price (in cents), volume and side (\"buy\" or \"sell\").</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>CREATE TABLE trades (\n    time TIMESTAMP,\n    user VARCHAR(32),\n    symbol VARCHAR(32),\n    price INTEGER, -- In ¢\n    volume INTEGER,\n    side VARCHAR(4) -- &quot;buy&quot; or &quot;sell&quot;\n);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0110","card":"q-fastapi-022-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"How does a FastAPI lifespan connect to the DB on startup and close it on shutdown?","a":"<p>Use an <code>@asynccontextmanager</code>. Code before <code>yield</code> is startup, <code>yield</code> blocks until shutdown, and <code>finally</code> guarantees the close.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    global _db\n    _db = sqlite3.connect(&#x27;trades.db&#x27;, check_same_thread=False)\n    try:\n        yield  # Server runs here\n    finally:\n        _db.close()  # Always close, even after exceptions</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0111","card":"q-fastapi-022-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"How do you register the lifespan with the app?","a":"<p>Pass it to <code>FastAPI</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0112","card":"q-fastapi-023-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"How do you give each request its own DB cursor?","a":"<p>Write a dependency generator. <code>with _db</code> commits, or rolls back on error.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_cursor():\n    with _db as cursor:\n        yield cursor</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0113","card":"q-fastapi-023-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"How does a handler use the <code>get_cursor</code> dependency?","a":"<p>Add <code>cursor=Depends(get_cursor)</code> as a parameter. <code>Depends</code> makes FastAPI call <code>get_cursor()</code> for each request.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.post(&#x27;/trades&#x27;)\ndef new_trade(trade: Trade, cursor=Depends(get_cursor)):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0114","card":"q-fastapi-023-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"Why does the trade handler use <code>side.value</code>?","a":"<p>It extracts the string from the Enum.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;side&#x27;: trade.side.value,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0115","card":"q-fastapi-023-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"How do you protect SQL queries from injection in the trades example?","a":"<p>Use <strong>parameterized queries</strong> with named placeholders such as <code>:user</code>. Never string-format SQL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>INSERT INTO trades\n    (user, time, symbol, price, volume, side)\nVALUES\n    (:user, :time, :symbol, :price, :volume, :side)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0116","card":"q-fastapi-023-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"Which validation rules does the <code>Trade</code> model apply?","a":"<p><code>user</code> and <code>symbol</code> need a minimum length of 3, <code>price</code> and <code>volume</code> must be greater than 0, and <code>side</code> is an Enum.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user: str = Field(min_length=3)\nprice: int = Field(gt=0)   # In cents</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0117","card":"q-fastapi-023-databases-lifespan-and-dependency-inject","sec":"fastapi-s023","q":"What does a trade request body look like?","a":"<p>JSON with user, time, symbol, price, volume and side, sent with <code>POST http://localhost:8000/trades</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n  &quot;user&quot;: &quot;warren&quot;,\n  &quot;time&quot;: &quot;2024-08-13T18:27:44&quot;,\n  &quot;symbol&quot;: &quot;MSFT&quot;,\n  &quot;price&quot;: 41360,\n  &quot;volume&quot;: 1000,\n  &quot;side&quot;: &quot;buy&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0118","card":"q-fastapi-024-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What is the task in the CSV-processing production-ready example?","a":"<p>Plug the security holes and add logging and metrics. The original read the whole body with no size or content-type check.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0119","card":"q-fastapi-024-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What does the <code>distance()</code> helper compute?","a":"<p>The euclidean distance in kilometers between two coordinates.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def distance(lat1, lng1, lat2, lng2):\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Return euclidean distance (in kilometers) between two coordinates.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    delta_lat = (lat1 - lat2) * lat_km\n    delta_lng = (lng1 - lng2) * lng_km\n    return math.hypot(delta_lat, delta_lng)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0120","card":"q-fastapi-024-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What constants does <code>distance()</code> use to convert degrees to kilometers?","a":"<p><code>lat_km = 92</code> and <code>lng_km = 111</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lat_km = 92\nlng_km = 111</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0121","card":"q-fastapi-024-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What does <code>parse_csv</code> return?","a":"<p>It sums <code>distance()</code> between consecutive rows and returns the count, the total distance and the average speed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return count, total_distance, speed</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0122","card":"q-fastapi-024-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"How does <code>parse_csv</code> compute average speed?","a":"<p>Total distance divided by the duration in hours.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>duration_hours = (end_time - start_time).total_seconds() / (60 * 60)\nspeed = total_distance / duration_hours</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0123","card":"q-fastapi-024-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What size limit does the hardened CSV server set?","a":"<p>5 MB.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>MAX_CSV_SIZE = 5 * (1 &lt;&lt; 20)  # 5 MB</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0124","card":"q-fastapi-025-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"How does the <code>@timed</code> decorator log a metric?","a":"<p>It wraps an async function, times it with <code>perf_counter()</code>, and logs the duration in a <code>finally</code> block so it is always logged.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@wraps(fn)\nasync def wrapper(*args, **kw):\n    start = perf_counter()\n    try:\n        return await fn(*args, **kw)\n    finally:\n        duration = perf_counter() - start\n        logging.info(f&#x27;[metric:{fn_name}.time] %.3f&#x27;, duration)\nreturn wrapper</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0125","card":"q-fastapi-025-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"In what order do you stack <code>@app.post</code> and <code>@timed</code>?","a":"<p><code>@timed</code> goes directly under <code>@app.post</code>, next to the function. Otherwise the route registers the unwrapped function.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.post(&#x27;/run&#x27;)\n@timed  # Must be BELOW @app.post, otherwise the route registers the unwrapped function</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0126","card":"q-fastapi-025-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What does the hardened CSV server do when the content type is not <code>text/csv</code>?","a":"<p>It logs the error and raises <code>406 NOT_ACCEPTABLE</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raise HTTPException(HTTPStatus.NOT_ACCEPTABLE, detail=&#x27;not a CSV&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0127","card":"q-fastapi-025-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"What does the hardened CSV server do when the file is too large?","a":"<p>It logs the error and raises <code>413 REQUEST_ENTITY_TOO_LARGE</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raise HTTPException(HTTPStatus.REQUEST_ENTITY_TOO_LARGE, detail=&#x27;file too large&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0128","card":"q-fastapi-025-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"Which fixes make the CSV server production-ready?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Fix</th><th>How</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Size limit</td><td>reject over 5 MB with <code>413 REQUEST_ENTITY_TOO_LARGE</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Content-type check</td><td>require <code>text/csv</code>, else <code>406 NOT_ACCEPTABLE</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Logging</td><td><code>basicConfig</code> at module level; log bad format, oversized files and the result</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Metrics</td><td><code>@timed</code> decorator with <code>perf_counter()</code> and <code>finally</code> so duration is always logged</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Decorator order</td><td><code>@timed</code> sits directly under <code>@app.post</code>, next to the function</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0129","card":"q-fastapi-025-example-make-a-csv-processing-server-pro","sec":"fastapi-s024","q":"How does <code>run_stats</code> turn the request body into a CSV reader?","a":"<p>It reads the body, decodes it and wraps it in <code>StringIO</code>, then calls <code>parse_csv</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>data = await request.body()\nfp = StringIO(data.decode())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0130","card":"q-fastapi-026-7-quick-patterns-recap","sec":"fastapi-s025","q":"What is the FastAPI pattern for a handler and for query parameters?","a":"<p>A decorator ties a function to a verb and path, and type-hinted function parameters become query parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.get(&#x27;/path&#x27;)\ndef handler(): return {&#x27;key&#x27;: &#x27;value&#x27;}\n@app.get(&#x27;/logs&#x27;)\ndef query(start: datetime, end: datetime): ...</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0131","card":"q-fastapi-026-7-quick-patterns-recap","sec":"fastapi-s025","q":"What is the FastAPI pattern for a request body and a path parameter?","a":"<p>A Pydantic model parameter gives the body, and <code>{login}</code> in the route gives the path parameter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def create(item: Item): ...\n@app.get(&#x27;/users/{login}&#x27;)\ndef get_user(login: str): ...</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0132","card":"q-fastapi-026-7-quick-patterns-recap","sec":"fastapi-s025","q":"What is the FastAPI pattern for raw requests and responses?","a":"<p>Take a <code>Request</code>, await its body, and return a <code>Response</code> with a media type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>async def upload(request: Request):\n    data = await request.body()\n    return Response(content=data, media_type=&#x27;image/png&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0133","card":"q-fastapi-026-7-quick-patterns-recap","sec":"fastapi-s025","q":"What are the FastAPI patterns for streaming, custom errors and middleware?","a":"<p>Return <code>StreamingResponse</code> with a generator, register an exception handler returning <code>JSONResponse</code>, and use <code>@app.middleware('http')</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return StreamingResponse(generator)\n@app.exception_handler(MyError)\n@app.middleware(&#x27;http&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0134","card":"q-fastapi-026-7-quick-patterns-recap","sec":"fastapi-s025","q":"What are the FastAPI patterns for dependency injection and lifespan?","a":"<p>Use <code>Depends</code> for per-request dependencies and pass a lifespan function to <code>FastAPI</code> for startup and shutdown.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def new_trade(cursor=Depends(get_cursor)): ...\napp = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan_fn)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fastapi-f0135","card":"q-fastapi-026-7-quick-patterns-recap","sec":"fastapi-s025","q":"What does the course suggest as a next step after learning FastAPI?","a":"<p>Pick a real project that needs an API server, start small, and leave room to grow.</p>","hand":true}];
